SirenCosyVoice

Swift port of CosyVoice 3 for Siren, vendored from soniqo/speech-swift
(https://github.com/soniqo/speech-swift), Apache License 2.0, commit
cbad3be29480825707890490f446b19d7288be2d (25 Oct 2026). Copyright the
speech-swift authors. The full licence is in LICENSE.

CosyVoice 3 itself is by FunAudioLLM (Alibaba Tongyi Lab), Apache License 2.0.
The weights Siren downloads are aufklarer/CosyVoice3-0.5B-MLX-bf16 and
aufklarer/CamPlusPlus-Speaker-CoreML on Hugging Face.

Taken unchanged: Sources/AudioCommon, Sources/MLXCommon and
Sources/CosyVoiceTTS, except as listed below.

Changes made for Siren:
- Package.swift is new: only these three targets, on mlx-swift 0.32.3 or
  later (speech-swift pins mlx-swift below 0.32 through mlx-swift-lm).
- CosyVoiceTTS/CamPlusPlusMelExtractor.swift: the per-frame mean subtraction
  uses one buffer pointer that outlives each vDSP call, instead of
  `&melSpec + base` (a pointer only valid inside the `+`).
- Cancellation: the LLM token loop (LLM.swift), the flow-matching steps
  (FlowMatching.swift), the long-form segment loop (VoiceCloning.swift) and
  synthesis before the flow and before HiFi-GAN (CosyVoiceTTS.swift) stop
  when the calling task is cancelled, so Stop ends GPU work promptly.
- CosyVoiceTTS.swift: the speech-token budget is capped at 750 tokens (30 s
  at 25 Hz) on top of the existing 10x-content scaling.
- CamPlusPlusSpeaker.swift: `fromPretrained` takes the CoreML compute units
  (default unchanged, `.cpuAndNeuralEngine`); Siren passes `.cpuOnly`, since
  compiling the 15 MB encoder for the Neural Engine took about 97 s per launch.
